{"id":"44b44a4f-427a-49ad-8f7e-fc7869dc234a","object":"chat.completion","created":1784882946,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    import json\\n\\n    # Validate required fields\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be a dict\\\")\\n    if 'edges' not in case or 'communities' not in case or 'resolution' not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case missing required fields: edges, communities, resolution\\\")\\n\\n    edges = case['edges']\\n    communities_in = case['communities']\\n    gamma = float(case['resolution'])\\n\\n    # Build weighted adjacency (undirected)\\n    adj = {}\\n    for u, v, w in edges:\\n        w = float(w)\\n        adj.setdefault(u, {})[v] = adj.get(u, {}).get(v, 0.0) + w\\n        adj.setdefault(v, {})[u] = adj.get(v, {}).get(u, 0.0) + w\\n\\n    # Node list in stable order (sorted by ID)\\n    nodes = sorted(communities_in.keys())\\n\\n    # Compute node degrees\\n    degree = {}\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        deg = sum(adj.get(node, {}).values())\\n        degree[node] = deg\\n\\n    # Total edge weight (m) = sum of all edge weights / 2? Actually each edge counted twice in adjacency\\n    m = sum(degree.values()) / 2.0\\n\\n    # Initialize community membership (make a mutable copy) and community degree sums\\n    comm = {node: str(communities_in[node]) for node in nodes}  # ensure string\\n    comm_deg = {}\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        c = comm[node]\\n        comm_deg[c] = comm_deg.get(c, 0.0) + degree[node]\\n\\n    moves = []\\n\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        di = degree[node]\\n        cur_c = comm[node]\\n        # Skip if degree zero (no neighbors)\\n        if di == 0.0:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Build weight to each neighboring community from current perspective\\n        comm_weight = {}\\n        for nb, w in adj.get(node, {}).items():\\n            nb_c = comm[nb]\\n            comm_weight[nb_c] = comm_weight.get(nb_c, 0.0) + w\\n\\n        # Weight to current community (must be computed before any move that changes comm)\\n        w_cur = comm_weight.get(cur_c, 0.0)\\n        S_cur = comm_deg.get(cur_c, 0.0)\\n        term_cur = w_cur - gamma * di * (S_cur - di) / (2.0 * m)\\n\\n        best_gain = 0.0\\n        best_c = None\\n\\n        # Evaluate each candidate community (neighbors' communities, not including current)\\n        for c, w_c in comm_weight.items():\\n            if c == cur_c:\\n                continue\\n            S_c = comm_deg.get(c, 0.0)\\n            term_c = w_c - gamma * di * S_c / (2.0 * m)\\n            gain = term_c - term_cur\\n            if gain > best_gain or (gain == best_gain and best_c is not None and c < best_c):\\n                best_gain = gain\\n                best_c = c\\n\\n        if best_gain > 0.0 and best_c is not None:\\n            # Record the move\\n            moves.append({'from': cur_c, 'node': node, 'to': best_c})\\n            # Update community membership and community degrees\\n            comm[node] = best_c\\n            comm_deg[cur_c] = comm_deg.get(cur_c, 0.0) - di\\n            comm_deg[best_c] = comm_deg.get(best_c, 0.0) + di\\n\\n    # Build output communities dict (keys exactly as input, values as strings)\\n    out_communities = {node: comm[node] for node in nodes}\\n    return {'communities': out_communities, 'moves': moves}\\n\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) that returns a JSON object with communities (object with string values, keys from case.communities) and moves (array of objects with from, node, to). The task is a local moving phase (Leiden algorithm) using resolution and quality gains. However, the provided description mentions \"registered resolution-adjusted gain\" but doesn't specify how to compute it. From the fixture payloads, we see edges (list of [node1, node2, weight]), communities (initial assignment),